{"id": "unknown-2026-07-07-005", "date": "2026-07-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 28, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["outperform"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "Weekly price shock alert: Lyocell - week ended July 3", "content": "China and Pakistan fell 0.14 per cent while India held flat, leaving lyocell as Asia's one of stable major fibre with all three markets locked within a 0.14-point weekly range.\nLyocell outperformed polyester and viscose as disciplined supply kept prices firm despite softer pulp costs.\nStable pricing strengthens yarn pricing across Asia, while Pakistan's gas-cost shock limits mill profitability.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/weekly-price-shock-alert-lyocell-week-ended-july-3-311517-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-07-006", "date": "2026-07-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 28, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cambodia, China’s Hainan province vow to expand bilateral trade", "content": "China’s Hainan province and Cambodia have reaffirmed their commitment to expand trade and investment cooperation. \nCambodia’s commerce secretary Lim Lork Piseth met a delegation from the province, and both sides highlighted the strategic importance of the Hainan Free Trade Port as a gateway for deeper economic collaboration. \nPiseth outlined opportunities to expand market access for Cambodian products. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/cambodia-china-s-hainan-province-vow-to-expand-bilateral-trade-311513-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-07-007", "date": "2026-07-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 28, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam’s HCM City to cut logistics costs to 11-14% of regional GDP", "content": "Vietnam’s HCM City is rolling out a logistics development strategy to reduce costs to 11-14 per cent of its regional GDP by 2030—lower than the national target of 15-16 per cent. \nThe aim is to position the city as a modern logistics hub and strengthen its role in global supply chains. \nRing roads, new expressways, dedicated railway lines and upgraded waterways, are being planned. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-s-hcm-city-to-cut-logistics-costs-to-11-14-of-regional-gdp-311514-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-07-008", "date": "2026-07-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 28, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s Jharkhand unveils drafts of industrial, textile policies", "content": "India’s Jharkhand state has unveiled the draft versions of the Jharkhand Textile, Apparel & Footwear Policy 2026 and the Jharkhand Industrial Investment Promotion Policy 2026, seeking feedback from stakeholders. \nThe latter aims at aligning with key national initiatives, enabling the state to integrate into global value chains and promote high-value segments like tech textiles and MMF products. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-jharkhand-unveils-drafts-of-industrial-textile-policies-311511-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-07-009", "date": "2026-07-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 28, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Levi's Q2 to test apparel's new tariff-driven margin playbook", "content": "Levi's Q2 could become the apparel industry's first real benchmark for post-IEEPA tariff economics. \nWith just ~1 per cent China sourcing, a potential $35 million COGS benefit, $0.07 EPS upside and an $80 million tariff refund in play, its guidance will determine whether diversified sourcing now delivers a structural margin edge—and reshape sourcing, pricing and supplier strategies across global apparel.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/levi-s-q2-to-test-apparel-s-new-tariff-driven-margin-playbook-311510-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-07-010", "date": "2026-07-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 28, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["concerns", "delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton advances on US weather concerns, grain market rally", "content": "ICE cotton futures rose over 1.5 per cent, supported by US weather concerns and a rally in CBOT grain markets, marking the fourth gain in five sessions.\nLimited rainfall in US cotton areas and delayed crop development in India underpinned sentiment, while USDA lowered the US cotton crop's good-to-excellent rating.\nTrading volumes remained light despite the price rally.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-advances-on-us-weather-concerns-grain-market-rally-311515-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-07-011", "date": "2026-07-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 28, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh invites US firms to expand investment", "content": "Bangladesh has invited US firms to expand their investments in the country, assuring policy stability, equal treatment and a more business-friendly environment.\nPM's adviser Mahdi Amin made this request while addressing a programme marking the 250th anniversary of US independence. \nHe identified energy, textiles and high-value manufacturing as sectors with strong potential for expanded cooperation. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-invites-us-firms-to-expand-investment-311508-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
